--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/xbe/vm-query-fastpath/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# VM query boundary and work oracle
+
+Build with `NXDK_DIR=/path/to/nxdk make`. The 989 checks use only public APIs
+and owned fixed-address reservations. All seven MEMORY_BASIC_INFORMATION fields
+are asserted against captured public reference records, including sparse/mixed/noaccess and free-region boundaries and
+invalid high-address output preservation. No arbitrary output pointers or
+private page tables are read. Timings are diagnostic batch counter deltas;
+correctness acceptance never relies on timing. The synthetic 256-fragment
+workload is not a recorded game allocation layout.
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/host/vm-query-fastpath/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Actual-source VM query differential
+
+`python3 check.py SOURCE OUTPUT` compiles the production lookup, protection
+decoder and query against the frozen prior production functions. ASan/UBSan,
+38,061 cases, full output bytes/status/guards, mutex checks and explicit work
+budgets cover sparse and mixed PDE/PTE spans and zero/one/16/256 region lists.
+`--allow-baseline` runs the same semantic comparison before the patch; without
+that option the old implementation fails the intended one-list-walk assertion.
+Host pointer widths differ from Xbox. The public native fixture supplies the
+28-byte target-ABI check. Neither fixture reads proprietary implementation code.
